'use strict';
(globalThis.ABBATE_QUESTION_TRANSLATIONS||(globalThis.ABBATE_QUESTION_TRANSLATIONS={}))["en"]={"g-flurpruefung":["What is included in a visual and functional inspection before starting work?","Before the first mission of the day.","Check fuel level and vehicle color only.","Check brakes, steering, forks, tires and safety devices according to the operating instructions.","Carry out a test drive with the load raised.","The daily inspection includes the safety-relevant parts and functions according to the operating instructions."],"g-rueckhalt":["How do you deal with the existing driver restraint system?","The forklift truck has a mandatory restraint system.","Use it properly while driving.","Use only on uneven floors.","Deactivate it for short journeys.","The intended restraint systems must be used in accordance with the manufacturer's instructions; they provide particular protection in the event of tipping events."],"g-mangelmelden":["What applies to a forklift with a damaged fork?","When checking, you notice a clearly bent tine.","If possible, distribute the load to the other tine.","Only drive light loads until the next service.","Do not use the forklift and report the defect to the responsible person.","Damaged load handling equipment can fail; Safety-related defects require shutdown until clarification."],"g-einweisung":["You switch to a forklift with different controls. What is required before use?","The operation differs from your previous vehicle.","Device-related instruction and compliance with the operating instructions.","A short explanation from an uninvolved colleague is always enough.","No additional information if you have a forklift license.","A general qualification does not replace the necessary instruction on the device actually used."],"g-anbaugeraet":["You should use an attachment. What do you check first?","A new piece of equipment changes the way the load is picked up.","Whether the attachment fits the vehicle approval and the permissible load.","Only whether the device can be attached visually.","Whether the attachment can be installed without documentation.","Attachments can change the remaining load capacity and load center; Approvals and load capacity information must be checked."],"g-diagramm":["Why do you need the load capacity diagram?","A heavy load is present with the center of gravity far outwards.","To determine the shortest route.","To assess the maximum permissible load depending on the lifting height and load center.","To determine the tank capacity.","Permissible loads depend, among other things, on the load center distance and lifting height."],"g-lastschwerpunkt":["What typically happens when the center of gravity moves further forward?","A long load protrudes far in front of the forks.","The permissible load capacity may decrease.","The carrying capacity is always increasing.","The distance has no influence on the tipping moment.","A larger distance from the load center increases the tipping moment and can reduce the permissible load capacity."],"g-gabelabstand":["How should the forks pick up a suitable pallet?","You want to pick up an evenly loaded pallet.","With the tines as close as possible and only on one corner.","With such a large distance that the pallet tips over to the side.","With suitable tine spacing and sufficient undercarriage and support area.","The load must be supported securely and as evenly as possible across the forks."],"g-schieflast":["A load is stacked unstably. What is right?","Cardboard boxes can fall when lifted.","Start slowly; the charge stabilizes itself.","Before picking up the load, secure it sufficiently or have it reassembled.","Raise the load above head height so that it does not get in the way.","Loose or unstable cargo can fall and endanger people; carry out safety measures first."],"g-personen":["Can a person be lifted on ordinary forks?","A colleague wants to reach a light.","Yes, if the colleague wears a helmet.","No, only designated and permitted facilities can be used by people in accordance with special requirements.","Yes, if only a small height is approached.","Normal forks are not a personal work platform; Transporting and lifting people is subject to special requirements."],"g-transporthoehe":["How do you usually transport a pallet?","The road is clear and level.","With the load raised only as far as necessary and in accordance with the operating instructions.","With the load lifted as high as possible to be better seen.","With the lifting mast tilted strongly forward, regardless of the load.","A low transport position reduces the risk of tipping and collisions; The device instructions are decisive."],"g-kurvenfahrt":["Why is cornering quickly with a forklift truck dangerous?","You want to quickly exit a narrow path.","Because it just drains the battery faster.","Because the forklift automatically steers better.","Because lateral forces affect stability and can lead to tipping over.","When cornering, additional forces come into play; the speed must be adjusted to the load and conditions."],"g-ladebruecke":["What do you check before driving onto a loading bridge?","You should drive in a truck.","Just whether the path looks wide enough.","Load capacity, secure support and protection against shifting as well as securing the vehicle.","Just whether the lighting is on.","Loading bridges and vehicles must be secured against movement and suitable for the load."],"g-fussgaenger":["How do you behave at a confusing intersection with pedestrians?","Visual connections are restricted.","Drive at an appropriate speed, stop if necessary and ensure safe visibility.","Always claim the right of way when carrying a load.","Just honk and keep driving.","Pedestrians have special protection needs; Speed, visibility and communication must be adapted to the traffic route."],"g-batterieladen":["What should you pay particular attention to when charging a drive battery?","A battery charging station is used.","The charging location can be selected regardless of the manufacturer's instructions.","Open flames are permitted as long as the truck is stationary.","Suitable loading area, sufficient ventilation and manufacturer's specifications as well as fire and explosion protection.","When charging, hazards can arise from electrical energy, gases and chemicals; the protective measures provided must be adhered to."],"h-beauftragt":["Under what conditions are you allowed to operate an aerial work platform independently?","You should use a work platform in the company.","If you have a car driving license.","If you are suitable, instructed or qualified and commissioned by the employer.","If you have ever seen a work platform.","The employer must ensure suitability, qualifications and assignments in accordance with operational requirements."],"h-vorpruefung":["What should be checked before starting work with the aerial work platform?","The stage was outside overnight.","Visual and functional test according to manufacturer's instructions including safety devices.","Just the color and age of the stage.","Whether the work material is already on the platform.","Before use, the machine, controls, emergency functions and visible damage must be checked in accordance with the operating instructions."],"h-tragfaehigkeit":["What information determines the permissible load on the work basket?","Two people would like to take additional tools with them.","People are free to estimate the permissible total weight.","Only the weight of the heaviest person counts.","The load capacity specification for people, tools and material must not be exceeded.","The nominal load refers to the total permissible load, including any material carried."],"h-untergrund":["What do you consider before setting up a stage with supports?","You are working near a filled area.","Only within the reach of the boom.","Check the load-bearing capacity and evenness of the subsurface as well as suitable support according to the instructions.","On the lowest possible number of extended supports.","Insufficient ground or improper support can lead to loss of stability."],"h-wind":["Strong wind sets in. How do you go about it?","You find yourself with an outdoor stage.","Observe the manufacturer's limits and if they are exceeded, stop operation or lower the basket safely.","Extend the platform as far as possible so that it is more stable.","Only react if loose objects fall.","The wind conditions permitted by the manufacturer are operational limits; Wind can create dangerous additional forces."],"h-strom":["You have to work near an overhead power line. What is crucial?","A live line is in the work area.","A helmet replaces maintaining a safe distance.","Just isolate the basket and work without coordination.","Clarify the danger area and ensure necessary protective distances or other suitable measures.","Electrical flashover is also possible without direct contact; Necessary protective measures must be determined before the start of the operation."],"h-notablass":["Why does the emergency lowering procedure need to be known?","A failure of the normal control is possible.","So that in the event of a malfunction, safe rescue is possible according to the device.","So that the device runs faster in normal operation.","To replace regular testing.","Emergency controls, emergency lowering and rescue concepts must be known and functional before use."],"h-gelaender":["How do you achieve additional height in the work basket?","A montage point is just beyond your reach.","Climb onto the basket fence.","Place a board on the railing.","Use a suitable platform with sufficient working height; do not climb on railings.","Climbing the fence or improvised elevations endangers the fall protection."],"h-psaga":["What requirements apply to personal fall protection equipment?","You use a work platform for which a restraint system is provided.","Any anchor point outside the basket is always sufficient.","Observe risk assessment, manufacturer information and suitable anchor points.","Do not use any security if the basket has a railing.","Whether and which PPE is necessary is determined by the risk assessment, stage construction and operating instructions."],"h-verfahren":["Can the stage be moved with the platform raised?","The workplace is a few meters away.","Only if the model and operating conditions allow it according to the manufacturer's instructions.","Always, as long as everyone holds on.","No, never regardless of design and manufacturer approval.","The movement in the raised position depends on the device and is only permitted within the approved operating conditions."],"h-kollision":["What needs to be organized when working near cranes or other machines?","Moving parts could reach the work basket.","Nothing; the work basket is always visible.","Always drive the work basket over the other machines.","Coordinate work areas to avoid collisions or pinch points.","Simultaneous machine operation requires coordinated work processes and protection against collisions or jamming."],"h-einstieg":["How do you enter or leave the work basket?","You reach the basket at ground level.","Climb over the outside railing.","Via the intended access in a safe position according to the operating instructions.","Via a ladder placed next to it with the boom extended.","Intended access and manufacturer instructions must be adhered to; Uncontrolled climbing over poses a risk of falling."],"h-defekt":["The emergency stop facility does not work. What are you doing?","You will discover the defect during the inspection.","Do not use the platform and report the defect.","Continue working if normal controls are working.","Tape the switch so that no one operates it.","Failure of a safety device is a safety-relevant defect and prevents safe operation."],"h-sicht":["The driving movement cannot be seen due to an obstacle. How do you go about it?","You should move a mobile stage.","Drive slowly without visibility.","Just rely on the distance indicator.","Stop movement and ensure visibility or safe instruction according to operating instructions.","Before the procedure, people, obstacles and traffic routes must be safely surveyed."],"h-rettung":["What does deployment planning involve when working at greater heights?","The stage is used in a remote area.","Only the planned working duration.","A suitable rescue concept with accessible, trained people and emergency lowering procedures.","The assumption that the fire department will solve any problem immediately.","An effective rescue must be organized in advance, even if the normal controls fail."],"k-befaehigung":["What is required to operate a crane independently?","A new employee is supposed to take over crane work.","Suitability and required qualifications, instruction and corresponding assignment.","A car driving license is sufficient.","Watching once is enough.","Crane work may only be assigned to qualified and authorized persons; Equipment instruction is part of it."],"k-funktionspruefung":["What does it take to check the crane before the start of the shift?","You take over an indoor crane.","Just read the running time on the nameplate.","Check safety-relevant functions and visible defects according to the operating instructions.","Test the crane with maximum load without checking.","The mandatory operational control serves to identify dangerous defects at an early stage."],"k-traglast":["What is the significance of the permissible load capacity?","A load is to be lifted.","It is a non-binding recommendation.","It only applies when the hook is fully retracted.","The permissible load capacity for the respective operating condition must not be exceeded.","Permissible loads for certain types of cranes can depend on the radius, boom position and armament."],"k-personen":["What applies to people under suspended loads?","The load is moved over a work area.","The danger area must be kept clear; no one is allowed to step under the suspended load.","A helmet allows you to stay directly underneath it.","Short crossings are permitted if the crane is moving slowly.","Suspended loads pose a risk of falling and crushing; People must be kept out of the danger area."],"k-signale":["You can't see the attacker and you get contradictory signals. What are you doing?","The communication is unclear.","Continue the last drive command.","Stop the movement and clearly clarify the communication.","Set down the load faster, without consultation.","Safe load movements require clear signals and clear communication."],"k-sicht":["Who will provide support during transport if the crane operator cannot fully see the load path?","A hall pillar obscures the path.","A person who happens to pass by without prior agreement.","No one; only the hook is important.","A suitable, instructed person with clearly agreed understanding.","If the load path is not visible, appropriate instruction or another safe solution is required."],"k-ruck":["Why should jerky crane movements be avoided?","A heavy load begins to swing.","They create additional dynamic stresses and can destabilize the load.","They basically reduce any pendulum movement.","They always increase the nominal load capacity.","Acceleration and braking forces increase the strain on the crane and slings."],"k-sperrbereich":["What should you check before swinging a load in a shared area?","Other employees work nearby.","Whether the load visually matches the crane.","Whether the danger area is secured and no people are at risk.","Whether the load can be carried as high as possible above everyone.","The swivel and load paths must be free of unprotected people."],"k-stuetzen":["What is crucial for a mobile crane with outriggers?","A crane is placed on partially filled ground.","Just the width of the road.","The color of the support plates.","Load-bearing base as well as support and load distribution according to installation and manufacturer instructions.","The installation has a significant influence on stability, especially in changing ground conditions."],"k-wetter":["A gust of wind causes the load to sway significantly. What is right?","You work outdoors.","Stop movement safely and observe permissible operating conditions.","Quickly accelerate the movement.","Continue to lift the load despite exceeding the manufacturer's limits.","Wind and swaying movements can destabilize the load and crane; Application limits must be adhered to."],"k-freileitung":["What applies when using cranes near overhead electrical lines?","Boom or load could approach the line.","With a non-conductive load, clearances are unimportant.","Clarify the danger area and necessary protective measures with those responsible before starting work.","Only rely on the crane operator's own reaction.","There are dangers from contact and voltage flashover; safe protective distances or other measures are required."],"k-sichern":["What do you do before you leave the crane?","Work is interrupted.","Let the load hang suspended.","Leave the crane unattended with the drive running.","Lower the load safely and secure the crane according to the operating instructions.","Suspended loads must not be left uncontrolled; The crane and load must be parked safely."],"k-lastanschlag":["How do you know whether the sling used is suitable?","The load should be lifted using a lifting strap.","In terms of marking, load capacity, condition and suitability for the type of attachment.","Just by the color of the lifting strap.","Because it was already used yesterday.","Load capacity and condition must be sufficient, taking into account the attachment conditions."],"k-stopp":["A person unexpectedly enters the load path. What are you doing?","The crane is currently moving a load.","Stop the movement safely immediately and have the danger area cleared.","Just give a warning signal and keep driving.","Raise the load higher and drive over it.","People must be protected from load movements; If there is an immediate danger, the movement must be stopped."],"k-neuerkran":["You will receive a crane with an unknown control. What is right?","The controls are different than before.","Try the usual keys if you suspect.","Allow someone else without training to drive ahead.","Receive the necessary device-related instruction before independent use.","Even experienced crane operators need knowledge of the specific controls used, protective devices and limits."],"a-kennzeichnung":["How do you know the permissible load capacity of a sling?","You want to choose a sling.","The smell of the material.","On the appropriate, legible load capacity marking and manufacturer's information.","On the length of storage time.","The permissible load capacity is determined by labeling and operating conditions."],"a-sichtpruefung":["You notice a clear cut in the lifting strap. How do you go about it?","The band is supposed to carry a load.","Do not use the tape and send it for testing or rejection.","Cover the cut with tape.","Only use it for particularly light loads.","Damaged textile slings can fail and must be assessed according to the discard criteria."],"a-neigungswinkel":["What happens if the angle of inclination of the sling strands is greater than the vertical?","A two-strand hanger spreads out more.","The strand forces always decrease.","The strand forces remain the same.","The forces in the strands increase; Permissible angles and load capacities must be adhered to.","As the spread increases, the tensile force per supporting strand increases."],"a-schwerpunkt":["Why do you need to know the center of gravity of the load?","The load is built up unevenly.","So that the load remains stable when being lifted and does not tip over uncontrollably.","To select the color of the slings.","So that the load can be rotated faster.","Unfavorable attachment points or the position of the center of gravity can lead to tipping, slipping or sloping slopes."],"a-kantenschutz":["A lifting strap lies against a sharp component edge. What should be done?","The component should be lifted.","Raise the load quickly before the belt is damaged.","Use suitable edge protection and check the type of attachment.","Only clean the load surface with a cloth.","Sharp edges can damage supporting fibers; the slinging equipment must be protected accordingly."],"a-haken":["What do you pay attention to when attaching a sling?","You use a cargo hook.","Place the sling on the side of the hook tip.","Keep the safety flap open permanently.","Load the hook as intended in the base of the hook and observe safety devices.","Impermissible load on the tip of the hook and a lack of securing can lead to it being unhooked."],"a-knoten":["Can you shorten a lifting strap that is too long with a knot?","The stop length doesn't fit.","No; Only use a suitable, approved type of sling or suitable slinging equipment.","Yes, if the knot is pulled very tightly.","Yes, as long as the load is currently stationary.","Knots can significantly weaken textile slings and are not permitted improvised length adjustments."],"a-probehub":["Why is a load initially lifted carefully?","You want to transport safely.","So that she can commute as quickly as possible.","To check the position of the slings, stability and center of gravity.","Because the load capacity increases automatically.","A controlled first stroke helps to detect incorrect stops and unstable load positions."],"a-lastweg":["Where are people allowed to stay while the load is being transported?","The load is moved with a crane.","Directly under the load with a protective helmet.","On the burden if they can hold on.","Outside the danger area and not under suspended loads.","Even with careful attachment, there are still dangers from falling or swinging loads."],"a-haende":["How do you avoid crush injuries when weaning?","The load approaches the support surface.","Keep hands and feet out of the crushing area and use appropriate aids.","Hold the load with your bare hand.","Stand between the load and the wall to correct the position.","Dangerous pinch points arise between the load and the support."],"a-vierstraenge":["What applies to load distribution on a four-leg suspension without load compensation?","A rigid load is attached.","All four strands inevitably carry the same amount.","Without proof of uniform distribution, the load-bearing capacity may not be used as a general estimate for four equally loaded strands.","The angle of inclination is then irrelevant.","Unequal strand loading is possible with rigid loads; The design and permissible load capacity must take this into account."],"a-chemikalien":["What applies when using textile slings in contact with chemicals?","You are working with an unknown liquid.","The color of the band reliably shows its durability.","Each textile band is resistant to all chemicals.","Check durability and manufacturer information; Do not use unsuitable means.","Chemicals can attack slings and unnoticed reduce their load-bearing capacity."],"a-aufbewahrung":["How are slings stored after use?","The mission is over.","Clean, dry and protected from damage according to manufacturer specifications.","Stuck on the ground under an unprotected load.","On any sharp outdoor hook.","Appropriate storage prevents premature wear and makes visual inspection easier."],"a-auswahl":["What should be particularly taken into account for sensitive or sharp-edged loads?","A painted machine component is to be moved.","Just the transport speed.","Suitable slings and protective measures for the load surface and edges.","Regardless of the load, always the same steel cable.","The type of attachment and material must match the geometry, surface and hazard."],"a-abstimmung":["The crane operator has no view of you. How do you give instructions?","You are assigned as an attacker.","You wave at will until a movement begins.","You just give one call and walk away.","Via clearly agreed signs or other reliable communication.","Attackers and crane operators must communicate clearly; If it is unclear, the movement must be stopped."],"b-qualifikation":["What does a person need to safely operate a hydraulic excavator during operation?","A new person should take over construction site work.","Appropriate qualifications, device-related instruction and required assignment.","Only a car driving license.","Just a quick observation of the operation.","The employer must ensure the necessary qualifications and instruct the operator appropriately for the task."],"b-pruefung":["What is included in daily machine inspection?","You take over an excavator.","Check the paint color and seat upholstery.","Visual inspection and functional tests according to the operating instructions, for example for leaks and damage.","Move the boom at full speed until it stops.","Damage to the hydraulics, chassis and safety devices can lead to serious accidents."],"b-leitungen":["What needs to be known about underground pipes before excavating?","You should dig a ditch.","Only the approximate depth of the planned excavation pit.","The color of the above-ground markings is sufficient.","Clarify the location of possible lines and determine suitable security and exploration measures.","Electricity, gas or water pipes can have life-threatening consequences if damaged."],"b-schwenkbereich":["How do you protect people in the swing area of ​​the excavator?","You pick up material with the boom.","Cordon off or secure the danger area and keep people away.","Before pivoting, move the shovel slowly.","Drive over the area over the heads.","Swivel superstructure and implements create crushing and impact hazards."],"b-boeschung":["What is important when working near the edge of an excavation pit?","The excavator is standing on established or filled ground.","The digging depth alone determines the permissible placement.","Pay attention to the load-bearing capacity and securing of the edge as well as the required distances according to the risk assessment.","Drive as close to the edge as possible to save range.","If there is insufficient clearance or stable ground, the embankment may fail and the machine may fall."],"b-standsicherheit":["Why are slope and ground crucial for use?","The construction site is on a slope.","The machine is equally stable on any surface.","Tracked undercarriages eliminate any risk of tipping.","Unevenness and slopes can affect stability; Observe application limits.","The stability and tipping safety depends on the floor, equipment, load and machine position."],"b-wechselgeraet":["What do you check after changing an excavator bucket using a quick coupler?","A new attachment was installed.","Whether it is correctly locked and secured according to the operating instructions.","Just whether the color of the shovel matches.","Whether the hydraulics work as quietly as possible.","Faulty locks can cause attachments to fall."],"b-heben":["What should you pay attention to when lifting a freely hanging load with an excavator?","The excavator is used for lifting operations.","Only the usual digging force is decisive.","Observe the permissible lifting load, suitable attachment points and prescribed protective devices.","The load can be hooked onto the teeth of the bucket.","Lifting is only permitted within the intended operating conditions with suitable equipment."],"b-rueckwaerts":["You have to reverse, but you can't see the path. What is right?","Other workers are nearby.","Drive off carefully without visibility.","Just honk and keep driving.","Stop, ensure visibility and the danger area or organize suitable instructions.","Reversing must not endanger people; limited visibility requires additional measures."],"b-kabel":["The boom could come close to an overhead power line. What are you doing?","You work on a tight construction site.","Clarify the danger area and suitable protective measures with those responsible beforehand.","Ignore the line if the boom is painted.","Only move the boom particularly quickly.","Electrical hazards arise from contact and flashover; safe distances and protective measures are necessary."],"b-verlassen":["How do you park the excavator before leaving?","You take a break.","Leave the boom floating freely.","Set down work equipment safely and secure the machine against movement and unauthorized use.","Leave the engine running and the cab open.","Lowered work equipment and protection against unintentional movement reduce the risk of accidents."],"b-hydraulik":["You notice hydraulic oil under high pressure on a damaged line. What is right?","A line is leaking.","Feel the leak with your hand.","Attach a new clamp under pressure.","Shut down the machine safely, allow the pressure to be reduced and arrange for repairs to be carried out by authorized specialist personnel.","Hydraulic fluid under high pressure can cause serious injuries; never check for leaks by hand."],"b-unterbau":["What is the danger of driving on unstable surfaces?","The ground is soft after rain.","The machine can sink, slide or tip over.","The drive automatically becomes wider.","This makes the swivel range safer.","Insufficient load capacity can significantly impair stability and driving safety."],"b-arbeitsgeraet":["Can someone work under a raised implement?","A person wants to control something under the shovel.","Yes, when the engine is idling.","No, not without the required safe support and securing of the work equipment.","Yes, if the person is wearing a safety helmet.","Hydraulic equipment can sink; Maintenance work requires secure work equipment."],"b-geraeteart":["You switch from a hydraulic excavator to a wheel loader. What is required?","Operation and movement behavior are different.","Just the same footwear.","A test drive without instructions.","The qualification or instruction required for the new machine type.","The qualification must match the type of machine used and the specific operational requirements."],"g-neigung":["You are driving a loaded forklift on an incline. What is important?","The route has a clear gradient.","Always guide the load downhill, even if it is heavy.","Guide the load uphill and observe operational guidelines for driving on inclines.","Regardless of the direction of travel, raise the fork to the maximum.","On inclines and descents, the load must always be carried uphill; The vehicle and operating instructions must be observed."],"g-gabelabsenken":["Why does the fork have to be lowered when parking?","The forklift is parked for a break.","So that others can use the fork to climb up.","So that the fork remains more visible from a distance.","So that lifting the load does not pose an unnecessary risk of tripping or injury.","Lowered load handling devices reduce the risk of accidents due to protruding or unsecured forks."],"g-fahrerwechsel":["A colleague would like to borrow the forklift. What must be present?","The colleague only has verbal permission from you.","He must have the necessary qualifications and a company mandate.","Your own assignment automatically applies to him too.","A private car driving license is sufficient for any business.","Independent leadership is tied to personal suitability, training, qualifications and operational assignment."],"g-ladungssicherung":["A pallet contains loose, stacked boxes. What is right?","A cardboard box can fall down while driving.","Secure the load against slipping and falling before transport.","Only drive slowly on particularly uneven ground.","Compensate for loose boxes with a higher fork position.","The load must be stable and secured against falling before it is transported with the industrial truck."],"g-bodenbelastung":["In front of you is a blanket with limited load-bearing capacity. How do you decide?","The route leads over an intermediate level.","Just pay attention to the weight of the truck without load.","Clarify the permissible floor load for forklifts and loads.","Drive with momentum so that the ceiling is under load for a shorter period of time.","What is relevant is the total actual stress on the area, including vehicle, load and dynamic influences."],"g-verkehrswege":["A marked footpath crosses your path. What is right?","Pedestrians can access the crossing at any time.","You can always claim priority with the horn.","You are allowed to drive over the marking without being observed.","Adjust your speed, pay attention to pedestrians and only continue driving when the path is clear.","Traffic routes must be driven with consideration for people; Warning signs do not replace safe visibility and a clear route."],"g-parkbremse":["You park a forklift on level ground. What does that include?","You want to leave the driver's seat for several minutes.","Park, apply parking brake and secure against unauthorized use.","Only leave the vehicle in neutral position.","Leave the fork at head height so that no one touches it.","Before leaving, the truck must be safely stopped and secured against unintentional movement."],"g-typenschild":["Which information is binding when it comes to the load on a forklift truck?","You want to pick up a heavy machine.","The estimated load capacity based on the vehicle size.","The manufacturer's information in the load or load capacity diagram.","The weight of the last pallet transported.","The permissible load is determined by the manufacturer's information and depends, among other things, on the load center and lifting height."],"g-tore":["You approach a low passage with a forklift. What are you checking?","There is a towering load on the vehicle.","Whether passage including the load and attachment is possible safely.","Only the height of the fork carriage without load.","Whether you can drive through faster before the gate closes.","Before passages, the clear height and width as well as dimensions of the load and vehicle must be taken into account."],"g-reifen":["During your daily check you find a badly damaged tire. What are you doing?","Safety-relevant damage is visible on the tire.","You drive slowly until your regular maintenance appointment.","You increase the tire pressure and keep driving.","You do not take the vehicle into operation and report the damage.","Damaged tires can impair stability and handling; the defect must be clarified before use."],"h-absperren":["Employees walk past under your work platform. What is necessary?","There is a danger from falling tools.","A suitable protective or restricted area under the workplace.","Just a notice when you first pass by.","Store tools as far away from the edge of the basket as possible.","A work area under elevated workstations must be secured against danger from falling parts."],"h-werkzeuge":["How do you transport tools in the work basket?","Several small tools are needed at height.","Place them loosely on the railing so they are within easy reach.","Store and secure in such a way that they do not fall down or impede operation.","Attach to the outside of the railing in your pocket.","Loose objects can fall and endanger people; secure storage is required."],"h-abstuetzung":["A support stands on a manhole cover. What needs to be checked?","You want to raise the platform.","Just make sure the lid is dry.","Whether the load can be absorbed safely at that point.","Whether the other supports do not need to be used.","The subsoil and contact areas must be able to safely absorb the supporting forces; Covers must be assessed separately."],"h-notaus":["When should the emergency stop device be used?","A dangerous movement immediately occurs.","Only at the end of a regular shift.","For stopping in acute danger according to the operating instructions.","As a replacement for the planned lowering.","The emergency stop is used to avert danger, not the usual control or normal shutdown."],"h-schraegstellung":["The stage tilt warning responds. How do you react?","The machine is on an inclined surface.","You ignore the warning at low working heights.","Despite the warning, you drive to the highest lifting position.","You stop and bring the stage into a safe condition according to the manufacturer's instructions.","Tilt warnings may indicate inadequate stability; further movements must not increase the danger."],"h-umgebung":["What needs to be organized when setting up near a traffic area?","Vehicles can touch the stage.","Protection against collisions and appropriate traffic guidance.","Swing the work basket as far as possible over the road.","Just a warning call before you boot up.","Aerial work platforms must be protected against collisions with road users; the installation must be secured accordingly."],"h-ueberlast":["The overload warning in the basket is triggered. What are you doing?","Additional tools were invited.","Finish work at higher speed.","Establish the permissible basket load and follow the manufacturer's instructions.","Switch off the warning signal permanently.","The maximum permissible load on the basket, including people and material, must not be exceeded."],"h-quetschen":["You drive the basket close under a roof. Which danger is particularly important?","There is little space left above the basket.","Clamping or crushing between the basket and the structure.","That the engine consumes more fuel.","That the direction of travel always reverses automatically.","Tight spaces above or next to the work basket can cause serious crush injuries."],"h-stromausfall":["The stage remains at a great height without a main drive. What is right?","The normal basket control no longer responds.","You climb down the boom without safety.","You wait until the end of your shift without being informed.","Initiate the prepared rescue using trained people and emergency lowering.","Safe rescue must be planned for disruptions; Trained people must know emergency functions."],"h-transportstellung":["How do you set the stage for a transport?","The aerial work platform is loaded onto a suitable vehicle.","Bring the boom and platform into transport position according to the operating instructions.","Tie down the platform as far out as possible.","Leave supports extended so it takes up more space.","The prescribed transport position and load securing are based on the manufacturer and transport specifications."],"k-bremsprobe":["What does a functional test of the crane brake show before use?","You want to be able to hold a load securely.","Whether the brake stops and holds the movement as intended.","Just whether the cabin lighting works.","Whether the hook can automatically hold a load.","Before use, safety-relevant functions must be checked according to the specifications."],"k-schraegzug":["Can you pull a sideways load at an angle with the crane?","The hook is not vertically above the load.","Yes, if the crane still has load reserve.","No, loads must not be pulled using impermissible diagonal pulls.","Yes, if the slings are particularly short.","Diagonal pulling can cause uncontrolled movements and additional strain on the crane and slings."],"k-verhakt":["A load hangs on the substructure. What is right?","Resistance is felt when lifting.","You keep lifting until it comes away.","You move the load sideways jerkily.","You stop and have the fastening or blockage safely removed.","Stuck loads must not be torn loose by force, as unacceptable forces can arise."],"k-anzuheben":["What do you check when briefly lifting a suspended load for the first time?","The load lifts a few centimeters from the ground.","Whether it hangs in balance and the stop is secure.","Whether a person can put themselves directly under the load.","Whether the crane becomes more stable by turning quickly.","Brief controlled lifting is used to check attachment, balance and safe load behavior."],"k-lastweg":["Where should the transport route of a crane load be?","Several workplaces are under the possible load path.","If possible, above occupied workstations.","On a planned, clear path with no people at risk.","Always diagonally through the busiest area.","Load routes must be organized in such a way that people are not endangered by suspended loads."],"k-signalverlust":["The radio connection to the marshal breaks down. What are you doing?","You cannot see the load path itself.","You continue the movement slowly.","You experimentally swing in the previous direction.","You stop the movement until there is a clear, secure understanding.","If there is a lack of communication, confusing load movement may not continue."],"k-haken":["The safety hook does not close reliably. What is right?","During the inspection, a defective closure is noticed.","The error must be corrected professionally before further use.","You tie the clasp tight with a cable tie.","You only use the hook for light loads.","Defective securing devices on load hooks can lead to slings becoming unhooked and must be remedied."],"k-zugrichtung":["What is important for the vertical support of a load?","The load is to be lifted from a machine.","The crane hook should be aligned above the center of gravity of the load.","The hook should be positioned as sideways as possible.","The load must be pushed before lifting.","A force effect that is as vertical as possible above the load center avoids impermissible lateral forces and uncontrolled swinging out."],"k-wartung":["An unusual grinding noise is noticed on the crane. How do you go about it?","The noise occurs when lifting.","Cover up the noise through higher speed.","Stop operations safely, report defects and have them resolved.","Continue working without notice until the break.","Noticeable changes can indicate safety-relevant damage and require an inspection."],"k-absetzen":["What must be guaranteed when lowering a crane load?","A heavy load is positioned on a surface.","The load may lie unsecured on an inclined surface.","Slings are removed while it is still floating.","The load is stable and secured against tipping or rolling away.","The load may only be released from the slinging gear after it has been safely set down and stability has been established."],"l-schwerpunkt":["Why does the center of gravity have to be known before striking?","An asymmetrically shaped machine is to be transported.","So that the load remains as balanced as possible when lifting.","So that the slings can be chosen as long as desired.","So that the permissible load capacity does not play a role.","The position of the center of gravity influences the load distribution and safe balance when lifting."],"l-etikett":["A lifting strap does not have a readable load capacity label. What is right?","The marking has become unrecognizable.","Estimate the load capacity based on the color.","Do not use the lifting strap until its suitability has been clearly demonstrated.","Only use the belt once for small loads.","Suitable markings are required for slings; Unexplained carrying capacity precludes safe selection."],"l-kantenschutz":["A textile band lies over a sharp steel edge. What is necessary?","The load has sharp edges.","Pull the band as tightly as possible without protection.","Perform the stroke faster.","Use suitable edge protection or other suitable slinging equipment.","Sharp edges can damage or cut textile slings; appropriate protection is required."],"l-spreizwinkel":["How does a larger angle of inclination affect the load on slings?","A load is lifted using two slanting ropes.","At less favorable angles, the forces in the strands can increase.","The strand forces disappear.","The angle has no influence on the stress.","With a less favorable stop angle, the forces per strand can increase; Load capacity tables must be observed."],"l-knoten":["Can a sling rope be shortened as desired using a knot?","The rope is too long for the planned load.","Yes, a tight knot improves load capacity.","No, only use approved shortening and anchoring methods.","Yes, if the knot is secured with tape.","Impermissible knots weaken slings and change their permissible load capacity."],"l-zeichen":["What applies to communication with the person operating the crane?","The load path is partially obscured.","Several people give different signals at the same time.","Clear, previously agreed signals are used.","Communication is never required with radio cranes.","Clear signs and clear responsibilities prevent dangerous incorrect movements."],"l-sichtpruefung":["When should slings be checked for visible defects?","You want to use a sling chain.","Before use, pay attention to any externally visible damage.","Only if an accident has already happened.","Only once when first purchased.","Before each use, the safe working condition must be assessed; Visible damage precludes safe use."],"l-drehung":["A lifted load begins to rotate uncontrollably. What are you doing?","The load moves in the load path.","You put your hand between the load and the wall.","You place yourself under the burden and hold on to it.","You keep your distance and let the movement stop in a controlled manner.","Uncontrolled load movements create crushing and impact hazards; People must leave the danger area."],"l-ablegen":["When can slings be removed from the load?","The load is placed on trestles.","If the load is stable and secured against tipping over or rolling away.","As soon as it touches the ground for the first time, regardless of its position.","While still hovering to save time.","Slings may only be removed after they have been set down safely and stably."],"l-ketten":["A chain sling has a severely bent link. What are you doing?","The damage is visible even before lifting.","Wrap the damaged area with wire.","Remove the chain from use and have it checked professionally.","Only raise the load half as high.","Deformed chain links are visible damage that can prevent safe use."],"b-einweiser":["What is important when visibility from the excavator is limited?","A part of the building obscures the driving area.","Appropriate visual measures or instruction and clear communication.","Just watch the hood.","Drive through the swivel area despite being invisible.","If visibility is restricted, hazards must be prevented through additional organizational and technical measures."],"b-aushub":["Where can excavated material be stored near a construction pit?","The edge of the pit must not be put at additional risk.","Pile up directly on the edge so that driveways remain clear.","Store at a sufficiently safe distance and according to construction site specifications.","Place on loose shoring without further testing.","Excavated material can endanger embankments and shoring due to additional loads; Safety distances must be maintained."],"b-personen":["Are people allowed to remain in the swing area while the excavator is moving?","A person wants to measure while panning.","Yes, as long as she wears a safety helmet.","Yes, if the excavator swings slowly.","No, the danger area must be clear before movement.","There is a risk of serious crushing and impact injuries in the swivel area; the area must be kept clear."],"b-ladung":["How do you transport material safely with a wheel loader?","A filled shovel should be driven across the yard.","With a suitable low transport position and a clear path.","With raised shovel for better visibility.","With open doors and strong steering angle.","A suitable transport position reduces the risk of overturning and improves driving stability."],"b-anbaupruefung":["What do you check after coupling an attachment?","A new shovel was attached.","Just the cleanliness of the paintwork.","The secure locking and function according to the operating instructions.","Just whether the device looks the same from the outside.","Incorrect locks on quick couplers can lead to the unintentional release of attachments."],"b-einstieg":["How do you get into the excavator cab safely?","The steps are dirty after rain.","Climb onto the cabin via the boom.","Get on the caterpillars in one jump.","Use designated steps and handholds and clean dirty steps.","Suitable climbs and safe holding points reduce the risk of slipping and falling."],"b-graben":["A trench wall shows cracks and is crumbling. What is right?","You work right next to the ditch.","Stop work and have those responsible secure the excavation pit.","Simply drive closer to the edge to close the ditch.","Deepen the trench further without protection.","Cracks and ground movements may indicate instability and require further safety assessment."],"b-betanken":["What do you pay attention to when refueling an earthmoving machine?","The tank is almost empty.","Secure the engine and ignition sources according to the manufacturer's instructions and avoid spillage.","Always refill petrol or diesel in the cabin.","Smoke while refueling when there is no wind.","Fire and environmental hazards when handling fuel require appropriate protective measures."],"b-laufwerk":["Why do the tracks and undercarriage need to be checked regularly?","You notice unusual vibrations while driving.","So that the machine can move faster.","Because damage can affect safe guidance and stability.","Because work is always permitted without visual inspection.","Damage to the drive can affect maneuverability, stability and safe operation."],"b-einweisen":["What is required when working near public pedestrian traffic?","An excavator works directly on the edge of a sidewalk.","Pedestrians should move through the swing area themselves.","Just stick a sign on the shovel.","Effectively cordon off the danger area and direct traffic safely.","Third parties must not enter the danger zone of earthmoving machines; Appropriate barriers and traffic routing are necessary."],"g2-fahrweg":["There is spilled liquid on the road ahead. How do you go about it?","The forklift would drive directly over the slippery area.","Stop driving and have the danger spot secured or removed.","Drive over the spot as quickly as possible with the fork raised.","Hope for drier tires and continue driving unchanged.","Contaminated routes endanger stability and must be adequately secured before driving on them."],"g2-sichtladung":["A high pallet blocks the view ahead. What is right?","You have to drive to a storage area and can't see the route.","Lift the pallet up until you can see underneath it.","Only drive using appropriate, safe methods, such as reversing with a clear view.","You can still drive on the road without a signpost or a clear view.","The direction of travel and visibility must enable safe observation of the traffic route; Loads must not replace visual inspection."],"g2-fussgaengerstop":["A pedestrian stops right next to the forklift. What are you doing?","The person is within the possible driving and pivoting range.","Overtake the pedestrian by accelerating briefly.","Drive past the person with the load raised.","Stop and only continue driving at a safe distance.","People must stay out of the danger area; If necessary, the journey must be interrupted."],"g2-hubmast":["You notice a damaged hydraulic line on the lift mast. What applies?","Hydraulic oil is visibly leaking from the implement.","Take the forklift out of operation and report the damage.","Check the leak by hand while lifting.","Only lift smaller loads until the shift is over.","Hydraulic damage can lead to uncontrolled movements; safe use is not guaranteed until the test."],"g2-lagerregal":["You want to store a pallet on a shelf. What do you check first?","The shelf level is high and the load capacity must be maintained.","Push the pallet onto the shelf as quickly as possible.","Check the shelf compartment, load weight and free storage space for suitability.","Estimate the total weight based solely on the number of boxes.","Shelves and load-carrying equipment must match the load and storage situation."],"g2-batterieschaden":["A forklift battery is damaged externally. What is right?","Before loading, cracks or unusual fluid are noticed.","Cover damage with adhesive tape and load immediately.","Let another person charge the battery without checking it.","Do not charge or use and inform the responsible specialists.","Damaged batteries pose electrical and chemical hazards and require professional assessment."],"g2-fahrerkabine":["What applies to loose objects in the driver area?","Tools are on the floor next to the control pedals.","Remove objects and keep the operating area clear.","Only hold the tool with one foot while driving.","Hide loose parts under the driver's seat.","Loose objects can block pedals and impair safe operation of the vehicle."],"g2-uebergabe":["You take over a forklift after a shift change. What does that include?","A colleague last used the vehicle.","Assume that the colleague has taken over all the checks.","Carry out the necessary inspection and inquire about known defects.","Start the journey without looking at the machine.","The person taking over must ensure that it is in a safe condition before use."],"g2-transportsicherung":["A tall object is loose on the pallet. How do you act?","The load could tip forward when braking.","Carry the fork particularly high so that the load remains stable.","Just take the curves slowly, go straight faster.","Set up the load in a stable manner and secure it against toppling or falling.","Loose loads must be stabilized before transport so that braking and driving movements do not cause them to fall."],"g2-arbeitsende":["What is important with an unattended forklift?","You end your shift and leave the area.","Park the vehicle safely and secure it against rolling away and unauthorized use.","Leave the key in so that colleagues can find the machine.","Leave the fork at eye level so that it is visible.","Safe parking includes lowered load handling and protection against movement and unauthorized commissioning."],"g2-bremsweg":["Why do you have to pay particular attention to the braking distance under load?","The forklift transports heavy goods through a warehouse aisle.","Always brake later with a heavy load than without a load.","Adjust speed to the visibility, ground and load conditions.","When braking, raise the load sharply to decelerate better.","Mass and road condition influence the stopping distance; adapted speed is key."],"g2-rampe":["What do you check before climbing a steep ramp?","The route may be too steep for the vehicle.","Drive on the ramp at maximum speed regardless of the gradient.","Drive over the edge of the ramp with the load raised.","Check the permissible gradient and safe operating mode from the vehicle specifications.","Only ramps within the intended operational limits may be used; Operating instructions and load control are decisive."],"g2-zinke":["A pallet is wider than the fork distance. What needs to be taken into account?","You plan on taking on an unusually large load.","Adjust the fork distance and mounting points to suit the load.","Only use one tine if the load is too wide.","Raise the load at an angle until it reaches the correct position.","Even and suitable load absorption reduces slipping and tipping."],"g2-betriebsanweisung":["What role does operational traffic regulation play?","Marked one-way and pedestrian areas apply in the warehouse.","With forklifts, only the rules of the public road apply.","Follow the specified routes and traffic rules.","Ignore markings once the vehicle is loaded.","Company routes and safety rules protect forklift traffic and people on foot."],"g2-nothalt":["The steering reacts unusually while driving. What is right?","The vehicle can no longer be controlled as usual.","Drive at higher speeds to make the steering more responsive.","Compensate for the error with particularly large steering deflections.","Stop in a safe place and have the vehicle checked.","Impaired steering endangers safe guidance; the machine must not continue to be operated uncontrolled."],"g2-anschlagkette":["You want to move a freely hanging load with a forklift. What applies?","A load should hang on a hook under the forks.","Only with an approved device and suitable load-carrying equipment.","Any chain will do if the load is not heavy.","Clamp the chain directly between both forks.","Freely hanging loads change stability; Manufacturer approvals and suitable facilities are required."],"g2-rollenlast":["A cylindrical component lies unsecured on a pallet. What are you doing?","The load may roll during transport.","Approach the pallet particularly jerkily.","Secure the component against rolling before the pallet is picked up.","Position the tines high enough that the component is not visible.","Round or rolling loads require reliable protection against changes in position."],"g2-pruefplakette":["How do you know whether the forklift can be used?","There is an inspection sticker stuck to the machine.","Any sticker always replaces the daily visual inspection.","A lack of clearance can be replaced by careful driving.","In addition to checking the vehicle, valid test status and operational approval must be taken into account.","Recurring testing and daily operational controls fulfill different safety functions."],"g2-licht":["The lighting in the warehouse suddenly went out. What is right?","You can no longer safely see obstacles in the path.","Stop driving until safe visibility is guaranteed.","Increase driving speed to leave the dark area.","Continue driving with the forks raised without visual inspection.","A route that cannot be safely overlooked must not be driven on without effective safety measures."],"g2-ueberhang":["A load extends far beyond the side of the fork. What are you checking?","You want to transport the pallet through a narrow gate.","Compensate for the lateral projection with a quick curve.","Assess clearance, stability and permissible load capacity before driving.","Drive the load at maximum speed regardless of its shape.","Overhangs increase collision risks and can alter stability and required traffic space."],"g2-wartungsbereich":["There are barriers in front of a maintenance area. How are you behaving?","Your usual route is temporarily closed.","Move barriers briefly and drive through unnoticed.","Drive directly through the work area under load.","Observe the closure and choose an approved alternative route.","Cordoned off areas may not be entered or driven through without permission."],"g2-bremsprobe":["When does a functional test of the service brake make sense?","You prepare the forklift before work.","As part of the required inspection before use.","Only carry out after a serious accident.","Only if the truck has already reached high speed.","The functionality of safety-relevant facilities is checked before use."],"g2-fahrzeuganhaenger":["You want to pull a trailer with a forklift. What is required?","The company is planning transport with an attached load.","Tie each trailer to a fork without checking.","Observe manufacturer approval, suitable coupling and permissible tensile load.","Just increase the tire pressure and drive off.","Train operation is only possible safely within the technical specifications and with a suitable connection."],"g2-rueckfahrt":["What is important when reversing with the forklift?","There is a confusing area in the warehouse aisle.","Always look only in the rearview mirror, regardless of the surroundings.","Drive without visibility as long as the horn has been pressed once.","Safely observe the route and people's area and, if necessary, have them instructed.","Reversing requires a clear view or effective additional safety measures."],"g2-lastentnahme":["You take a pallet out of a high shelf. What is right?","The palette may not be centered.","Pick up the load safely and stabilize it before lowering.","Allow the pallet to swing to the side as you pull it out.","Check underneath the raised pallet to see if it is damaged.","Controlled lifting and lowering prevents loads from falling and dangerous movements."],"h2-absenkweg":["Why does the area under an aerial work platform have to remain clear?","The basket is lowered and materials are placed underneath it.","Press materials down with the basket.","Only keep an eye on the operator's foot area.","Avoid the risk of crushing and collision when lowering.","The lowering area must not contain any people or obstacles that could become trapped."],"h2-transporthoehe":["How do you move a mobile stage over a low passage?","The clearance is lower than the extended boom.","Place the platform in a suitable transport position according to the operating instructions.","Leave the boom extended and move along under the ceiling.","Press the basket against the side of the door frame.","For travel movements, the overall height and transport position must match the manufacturer's specifications and the passage."],"h2-bodenoeffnung":["There is an unsecured opening in the floor next to the stage. How do you react?","A driving or support point is located near the opening.","Place a support directly on the edge of the opening.","Change the installation location or have the load capacity and securing checked professionally.","Only cover the danger point with a cardboard box.","Openings and edge areas can fail under support loads and must be effectively taken into account."],"h2-rettungsperson":["Why does a second person need to be familiar with the rescue procedure?","An operator could become incapacitated at the top.","So that work in the basket can generally take place without security.","So that the stage can be operated faster than permitted.","So that a safe rescue can be initiated in an emergency.","A rescue concept must take into account ground-based assistance in the event of a failure or emergency."],"h2-werkzeugabwurf":["What applies to tools at high altitude?","A loose tool could fall over the edge of the basket.","Secure tools so that they do not endanger anyone or fall down.","Simply place tools on the railing to reduce the load.","If necessary, throw tools down from the basket.","Falling objects endanger people below; Material must be stored safely."],"h2-trittstufe":["A box should serve as additional standing space in the basket. What is right?","Otherwise you will only barely reach the workplace.","Place the box on the railing and climb onto it.","Do not climb on improvised elevations; Use suitable work equipment.","Intentionally load the basket beyond the permitted height.","Improvised elevations impair the intended fall protection and are not permitted."],"h2-lastverteilen":["What do you pay attention to when there are several people in the work basket?","Two people are working in the basket with heavy tools.","Judge the load based solely on the tool size.","Store heavy tools directly on the protective railing.","Do not exceed the permissible basket load including people and tools.","The permitted load capacity includes all people, materials and tools in the basket."],"h2-abstuetzplatte":["When are additional shims for supports considered?","The installation floor can only bear a limited load.","If this is necessary for safe load distribution according to specifications.","In order to place the supports as close as possible to the edge of a construction pit.","In order to use any longer range without manufacturer information.","Sufficient contact areas are required for safe support forces."],"h2-baugrube":["A stage should be located directly at the edge of a construction pit. What are you checking?","The subsoil could give way laterally due to the excavation pit.","Extend the supports into the excavation pit.","Ensure sufficient safety distance and load-bearing capacity of the subsurface.","Only compensate for the risk by lifting the basket slowly.","Excavation pits can affect stability due to slope and subsoil failure."],"h2-witterung":["Icing sets in during use. How do you act?","Control surfaces and work area become smooth.","Raise the stage to avoid snow and ice.","Ignore the warnings as long as the platform is lit.","Interrupt work and reassess operating conditions according to the operating instructions.","Changes in weather can change liability, operability and safe limits of use."],"h2-aufbaukontakt":["A steel construction limits the basket path. What is important?","When lifting there is a risk of crushing between the basket and the carrier.","Plan movements so that your body and basket are not trapped.","Make the journey faster so that the basket passes by more quickly.","Push the construction with the basket to the side.","Pinch points between the platform and the environment require careful observation and controlled movement."],"h2-sicherheitsabstand":["When does the danger area of ​​a stage have to be cordoned off?","A public transport route passes under the site.","Only if an object has already fallen.","If third parties could be endangered by movement or falling objects.","Never, as the work basket basically prevents all dangers.","The area under and next to the stage must be protected against foreseeable hazards."],"h2-korbtor":["What applies to the work basket entrance door?","You are already at working height.","Leave the door open so you can get out quicker.","Tie the door permanently open with a rope.","Keep the door closed according to the locking mechanism provided.","The locks provided are part of the protective measures against falling from the work cage."],"h2-energieleitung":["What applies if an overhead line is not safely switched off?","You work with the aerial work platform near them.","Ensure specified safety distances and necessary protective measures.","Move the basket just in front of the line as long as it is not touched.","Trust in the plastic tires and work without any gaps.","Electrical flashovers are also possible without direct contact; Safety distances are required."],"h2-schwanken":["The work basket begins to swing unusually strongly. What is right?","The movement is no longer controlled.","Readjust uncontrollably with quick countermovements.","Stop movement and check cause or operating conditions.","Add extra people to the basket to make it heavier.","Unusual vibration may indicate unsuitable operating conditions or a malfunction."],"h2-ladegeraet":["A charging cable for the electrically operated stage is damaged. What are you doing?","When connecting, damaged insulation is visible.","Touch the damage with wet gloves.","Press the plug into the socket as hard as possible.","Do not start the charging process and have the cable checked professionally.","Damaged electrical wiring poses a risk of electric shock and fire."],"h2-gelaenderanbau":["Can you remove a railing yourself to get closer?","A component prevents people from approaching the work site.","Do not modify or remove protective devices on your own.","After lifting, unscrew the railing and install it later.","Continue working without a railing as long as someone is standing next to it.","Structural protective devices may not be changed without permissible specifications and safe replacement measures."],"h2-lastkran":["Can the platform be used as a crane to lift a load?","Material should be transported hanging freely next to the work basket.","Whenever the weight is less than your own body weight.","Only if the manufacturer and equipment expressly permit this special use.","Simply attach a hook to the railing and lift material.","Aerial work platforms are not automatically designed for crane work or additional suspended loads."],"h2-arbeitsvorbereitung":["What goes into preparing for a new location?","You don't know the construction site yet.","Just estimate the distance to the nearest parking lot.","Regardless of the surroundings, extend it completely immediately.","Assess hazards, soil, traffic routes, rescue and equipment suitability.","A location-related risk assessment is a prerequisite for safe operating conditions."],"h2-kabelschlaufe":["A power cable lies across the stage's path. What is right?","The cable could become trapped during the movement.","Clear the road and protect electrical cables from damage.","Use the cable with the wheels as a road threshold.","Raise the basket without checking the floor area.","Cables that are run over or crushed can cause electrical and mechanical hazards."],"h2-leitungsnaehe":["Who clarifies the protective measures on an electrical system?","The platform should work close to live equipment.","The person in the basket decides solely by eye.","Involve responsible authorities and implement coordinated protective measures.","The distance will only be determined after work has started.","Working near electrical systems requires planned and coordinated protective measures."],"h2-funkkommunikation":["Why do signals between the floor and the basket have to be clear?","A person on the ground assists with maneuvering.","So that several people can give contradictory instructions at the same time.","So that the emergency lowering can be tried out without instructions.","So that movements are only carried out after clear communication.","Clear communication reduces incorrect movements and collisions when maneuvering."],"h2-neuebedienung":["You switch to a different type of stage. What is required?","The operating functions differ significantly.","Device-specific instruction before independent use.","Just reading the company logo on the device.","A test drive with the basket already extended without instructions.","Qualification alone does not replace instruction in the specific device type."],"h2-steckanschluss":["What should you check before connecting a charger?","An electric aerial work platform needs to be charged.","Use any socket regardless of condition and fuse.","Check suitable connection and undamaged cable according to manufacturer's instructions.","Unplug the power plug regularly during charging.","Suitable and intact electrical connections protect against electric shock and fire."],"h2-absperrpersonal":["A person enters the cordoned off area during lifting work. What are you doing?","You can see a person directly under the work basket.","Continue driving if the person is wearing a protective helmet.","Drop a tool in their direction as a warning signal.","Stop dangerous movement and have the area cleared.","A barrier does not replace observation of the danger area during operation."],"k2-arbeitsplanung":["What should be included in work preparation before a crane operation?","Load, location and transport route have not yet been coordinated.","Lift the heaviest load first without further planning.","Only mark the shortest route on the hall floor.","Clarify the load capacity, slings, load path and danger area in advance.","A planned crane movement requires suitable load handling, safe routes and coordinated protective measures."],"k2-hakenposition":["How is the crane hook positioned over the load before lifting?","The attachment points are below the crane.","As vertically as possible above the center of gravity according to the stop.","Offset far to the side so that the load swings in more quickly.","In any case at the outer edge of the load, regardless of the center of gravity.","Vertical application of force and suitable anchor points reduce sideways movement and uncontrolled movements."],"k2-hakengabel":["A load hook shows a noticeable deformation. What applies?","The hook appears bent up from its usual state.","Bend the deformation back with the next load.","Stop crane operation and have the hook checked by an expert.","Only attach light loads and continue working.","Deformation may affect the safety of the hook; unauthorized further use is not permitted."],"k2-zugueberlast":["The burden is heavier than initially assumed. What are you doing?","New weight information arises during preparation.","Replace the safety reserve with faster lifting.","Ignore the load weight by attaching it to another point.","Determine actual load and recheck load limits.","Safe lifting requires reliable load data and compliance with all relevant load capacities."],"k2-arbeitskorb":["Can an ordinary crane hook easily carry people?","A person wants to get to a high place of work.","No, passenger transport requires permitted special facilities and measures.","Yes, if the person holds on to the sling rope.","Yes, as soon as the stroke is carried out particularly slowly.","The transport of people is only permitted under special conditions provided for this purpose."],"k2-bruecke":["A bridge crane moves along a shared hall path. What is important?","Employees stay under the transport route.","Drive with the load just above the employees' heads.","Effectively keep the load route and traffic area clear and secure.","Only use the warning horn instead of further measures.","People at risk must not be under suspended loads or in their transport path."],"k2-zweitekrane":["Two cranes work in an overlapping area. What is necessary?","Booms or loads could collide with each other.","Both crane operators work at the same time without prior agreement.","Movements are deliberately accelerated to avoid intersections.","Coordinate operations and take appropriate measures to prevent mutual threats.","Overlapping work areas require coordinated operational organization and suitable safeguards."],"k2-pruefbuch":["What is the significance of the mandatory recurring crane inspection?","The machine is used regularly in operations.","It supplements the operational control with the prescribed expert examination.","It permanently replaces any visual inspection before work begins.","It is only required after a crash.","Recurring inspections and ongoing operational controls have different tasks."],"k2-absetzflaeche":["The intended placement area is uneven. How do you act?","The load could tip over when placed.","Place the load on one corner and let it hang unchanged.","Prepare suitable, load-bearing and stable bases or surfaces.","Place one person under the load while lowering.","Placement areas must support the load safely and prevent dangerous tipping or rolling movements."],"k2-anfahrbereich":["Before the crane starts moving, there is one person in the travel area. What are you doing?","The route is blocked by a person.","Push the person aside with a short test drive.","Move off using the limit switch alone without visual inspection.","Only start movement when the danger area is clear and safe.","Driving and pivoting movements must not endanger people."],"k2-schlaffseil":["Why should the hoist rope not become uncontrollably slack when it is set down?","The load is on, the hook is lowered further.","So that the rope and hooks do not get jammed or subjected to uncontrolled loading.","So that the load can then be pulled laterally by the rope.","So that slings detach themselves from the hook.","Uncontrolled cable routing can lead to entanglements and dangerous load movements."],"k2-pendel":["A load being transported begins to sway. What is right?","The load moves laterally more than planned.","Compensate with quick countermovements and full speed.","Reduce movements in a controlled manner and calm commuting without people in the danger area.","Hold the swinging load with your bare hands.","Oscillating loads can affect people and facilities; calm movements reduce the risk."],"k2-funkakku":["The radio control of a crane has a weak battery. What applies?","The connection could break during lifting.","Lift a load quickly before the control fails.","If the connection is lost, move the load by pulling on the sling.","Ensure a reliable control connection before use.","Reliable control and communication are prerequisites for controlled crane movements."],"k2-mehrereanschlaeger":["Two people give different signals to the crane operator at the same time. What is right?","The signs contradict each other.","Interrupt movement and clarify clear responsibility.","Prefer the sign of the person further away.","Continue the movement according to your own feeling.","Crane drivers need clear and unambiguous communication, especially when load routes are confusing."],"k2-endabschaltung":["Why shouldn't a limit switch be misused as a normal stroke limitation?","The load is often moved up to the maximum lifting distance.","Limit switches generally allow faster lifting without visibility.","Limit switches are safety devices and do not replace controlled operation.","They should be hit as hard as possible with each stroke.","Safety devices serve to protect against dangers and must not be overused as planned."],"k2-wetterbeobachtung":["The wind increases significantly with a large area load. What is required?","A large component area acts like a sail.","Always raise the load higher so that the wind has less effect.","Replace the slings with thinner ones.","Assess wind and operational limits and adjust lifting if necessary.","Wind can generate significant additional forces and pendulum movements, especially with large-area loads."],"k2-ortswechsel":["What is important when moving a mobile crane to a new location?","Subsoil and support conditions change.","Check the stand location and support before picking up the load again.","Apply the settings from the previous location without checking.","Have the support readjusted during lifting.","Each installation location may have different ground and support load conditions."],"k2-betriebsbereich":["A crane is supposed to work across a street. What needs to be clarified?","Third parties could get into the danger area.","Only secure the road with a warning horn.","Required lockdowns, voting and protection measures in front of the hub.","Lift the load over vehicles as quickly as possible without securing it.","Safe traffic routing prevents undue risk to third parties from loads and crane movements."],"k2-hochheben":["After the test lift, a load hangs clearly crooked. What is right?","The focus was apparently misjudged.","Continue lifting so that the imbalance corrects itself.","Have one person pull the leaning load.","Set the load down safely and check the attachment and center of gravity again.","The test lift is used to detect incorrect attachment and unstable load positions before transport."],"k2-schwebelast":["Can you leave a lifted load hanging unattended?","The shift ends, but the load is still on the hook.","No, lower the load safely and secure the crane properly.","Yes, if the crane is locked against moving away.","Yes, as long as there is a warning sign on the ground.","In principle, suspended loads should not be left unattended."],"k2-mitnahme":["A colleague wants to ride on a crane load. What applies?","The load should be transported to a higher point.","Riding is permitted if the colleague wears a helmet.","People may not be transported on or attached to normal loads.","A ride is always permitted as long as the colleague is known to the crane driver.","Carrying people along with loads creates significant risks of falling and crushing."],"k2-warnsignal":["An operational warning system on the crane fails. What is right?","It is no longer possible to provide a warning before driving off.","Ignore the system when the engine is running.","Permanently replace the warning by tapping the housing.","Report a safety-related failure and interrupt operations according to instructions.","Required warning devices must be functional so that people are protected in a timely manner."],"k2-schneekante":["A mobile crane needs to be supported on frozen, uneven ground. What applies?","The soil may lose its bearing capacity as it thaws.","Assess the load capacity and support situation under actual conditions.","Frozen ground always has any bearing capacity.","Only place supports on small stones.","Temperature, humidity and subsoil structure influence the load-bearing capacity of crane locations."],"k2-laufkatze":["A trolley moves towards an obstacle. How do you act?","There is an object in the driving area.","Slowly push the object away with the load.","Stop movement in good time and have the obstacle safely removed.","Drive past the obstacle at increased speed.","Crane movements must be guided in such a way that no collisions with obstacles occur."],"k2-anschlagaufnahme":["You should pick up a load using an undesignated eyelet. What is right?","The eyelet could only be intended for mounting a cover.","Each eyelet is suitable for full crane load.","Only load the eyelet with two people at the same time.","Verify the load capacity and suitability of the anchor point before use.","Not every existing eyelet is a stable attachment point for crane loads."],"l2-seilbruch":["A wire rope shows several broken individual wires. What is right?","The breaking points are in the load-bearing rope area.","Do not continue to use lifting gear and have it professionally assessed.","Bend the wire ends back with your bare hands.","Continue using the rope if the load is particularly light.","Wire breaks can be a discard criterion; Damaged ropes must be assessed professionally."],"l2-schaekel":["What is crucial when using a shackle?","A shackle connects the sling and the load.","Replace the bolt with any nail.","Check for suitable load capacity, undamaged condition and correct bolts.","Estimate the load capacity based on the color.","Shackles must be appropriately sized, used completely and in the intended direction of loading."],"l2-tragfaehigkeit":["What do you have to consider when using multiple strands?","The strands run at an angle to the vertical.","Simply add up the load capacity of each strand as desired.","Only hang the load on the lightest strand.","Consider the load-bearing capacity of the entire type of anchor and angle.","The angle of inclination and the effective number of strands significantly influence the permissible load."],"l2-schweissnaht":["Can an improvised anchor point be welded to a load?","There are no suitable designated pick-up points for the load.","Only use properly designed and approved anchor points.","Any weld seam is sufficient without testing.","Insert a hook through an opening in the sheet metal.","Anchor points must be proven to be suitable for the forces involved in lifting."],"l2-einseitig":["A load is significantly heavier on one side. How do you go about it?","The center of gravity is outside the geometric center.","Leave all strands the same length regardless of the center of gravity.","Determine the center of gravity and adjust the position accordingly.","First raise the load to full lifting height.","If the center of gravity is off-center, loads can tip unexpectedly or individual strands can be overloaded."],"l2-kettenriss":["What applies to a chain sling with visible cracks?","There is a crack in one of the chain links.","Mark the crack with paint and lift it unchanged.","Wrap the link with wire and reuse it.","Remove the chain immediately and inform the responsible person.","Cracks in load-bearing chain links are safety-relevant damage and require decommissioning."],"l2-lastfuehrung":["How do you carry a large load when there is a risk of rotation?","The load can swing out to the side during lifting.","Use appropriate guidance devices and a safe distance.","Hold the load directly between your hands while driving.","Step under the load and align it from below.","Load guidance must not cause hands or bodies to get into the danger zone."],"l2-schnueren":["What is important when attaching the laces?","The sling is guided around a component.","Assume the same load capacity as any other type of anchor.","Observe the suitability of the type of attachment and the permissible load according to the marking.","Pull the sling gear together to any extent without checking.","The type of lace attachment can change the permissible load capacity and must be used correctly."],"l2-winkelmesser":["Why can't you ignore a flat strand angle?","Two sling lines run almost horizontally to the load.","A flat angle automatically makes the strand stronger.","The load is always distributed equally regardless of the angle.","High strand forces can exceed the permissible load capacity.","As the angle to the vertical increases, the stresses on the strands increase."],"l2-heisse-last":["What do you need to check for a hot load?","A steel part was recently heat treated.","Observe the temperature limits of the slings and suitable selection.","Every textile sling can withstand any temperature.","The labeling doesn't matter when it's hot.","Temperature can affect the permissible load capacity of slings."],"l2-abstand":["Can you put your fingers under the load when setting it down?","The load should land on a surface with millimeter precision.","Yes, if you wear work gloves.","No, keep your distance and use appropriate aids.","Yes, if the crane movement is particularly slow.","Parts of the body between the load and the base can become trapped."],"l2-verbindung":["A connecting link of the sling chain is not locked. What applies?","The fastener is missing.","Use the bolt without the lock when no one is watching.","Seal the element with adhesive tape.","Do not strike until the fastener is properly secured.","Connecting elements must be secured completely and in accordance with their design."],"l2-lasthaken":["What do you check when hanging on a crane hook?","Several slings should be guided into the hook.","Ensure secure fit and suitability of hooks and suspension.","Place slings on the tip of the hook.","Replace the hook lock with a cable tie.","The force must be applied as intended in the designated areas."],"l2-fasern":["A lifting strap shows severe roughening and fiber damage. What is right?","Supporting fibers are visibly damaged.","Cover the damage with another knot.","Separate out the lifting strap and have it checked by a specialist.","Then lift the load more quickly.","Damaged load-bearing fibers can significantly reduce the load-bearing capacity of a lifting strap."],"l2-anheben":["What applies immediately after the first centimeter of lifting?","The load is just lifting off its base.","Pull the load to its full height without control.","Check under the load whether the slings are tensioned.","Check the position of the stop, balance and movement behavior.","A controlled test lift makes possible instabilities visible before further transport."],"l2-lastgewichte":["The load weight is unknown. What is right?","The component has no weight marking.","Determine the loadable weight before selecting slings.","Estimate the weight based on the color of the load.","Use any double length sling.","Without a known or reliably determined weight, the suitability of the slings cannot be checked with certainty."],"l2-lose-teile":["There are loose tools on the load to be lifted. What are you doing?","Tools could fall when lifting.","Hold tools with one hand when driving.","Remove or effectively secure loose objects before lifting.","Raise the load a little faster so that nothing slips.","Loose objects can fall and endanger people in the area."],"l2-wind":["A large load is attached in strong winds. What applies?","The component offers the wind a large surface area to attack.","Raise the load without considering swaying movements.","Additional people should hold the load directly.","Assess wind conditions and refrain from lifting if the situation is unsafe.","Wind forces can affect load guidance and stability during transport."],"l2-unterlage":["Why are suitable documents important when weaning?","A round load would roll away on the ground.","Place the load firmly down and secure it against rolling if necessary.","Leave the load standing directly on the slings.","Only push the documents under the load after they have been set down.","Suitable supports prevent tipping over and unwanted movements when setting down."],"l2-transportweg":["What needs to be coordinated before the load is transported?","The load is moved over several work areas.","Just the expected duration of the hub.","Safe load path, communication and necessary barriers.","One person should show the way under the load.","Transporting loads requires safe traffic routes and clear coordination."],"l2-schutzschlauch":["What should you pay attention to when using slings with a protective hose?","A band lies against a rough edge.","Any thin cloth cloth replaces suitable edge protection.","A protective hose removes any permissible load limit.","Select protective equipment according to suitability and application requirements.","Protective equipment must match the material, the edge and the intended load."],"l2-reinigung":["A lifting strap was contaminated with an unknown chemical. What is right?","The tape can no longer be clearly assessed.","Stop use and clarify compatibility or condition professionally.","Clean with any solvent and continue lifting immediately.","Ignore the chemical while the tape is dry.","Chemicals can affect the strength of textile slings."],"l2-aufhaengung":["What do you check for multiple strands on the suspension link?","Two strands are placed together in a suspension.","A strand can move into the tip of the hook at will.","All connecting elements must be suitable and arranged as intended.","A ring with a crack can be used for small loads.","Stop and connecting elements must be load-bearing and correctly arranged."],"l2-einweiserrolle":["What applies if the attacker and the crane operator have no line of sight?","A carrier blocks the view of the drop point.","Coordinate by calling several people without responsibility.","Move the load based on noise without instruction.","Organize clear, secure communication and stop it if it is unclear.","Lack of visibility must be compensated for by effective coordination and secure communication."],"l2-ausserbetrieb":["A damaged sling was sorted out. What else is important?","It remains freely accessible alongside ready-to-use resources.","Secure against further accidental use and inform the responsible person.","Return the product unmarked to inventory.","Only use it again when carrying a particularly light load.","Discarded slings must be reliably protected before further use."],"b2-schwenkradius":["Why is the rear swing radius of an excavator critical?","The tail moves over a limited work area.","Third parties can be caught by the swinging superstructure.","The swing radius has no influence on people next to the machine.","The rear always only moves in the direction of travel.","When pivoting, a danger area also arises behind the machine."],"b2-verkehrseinweiser":["How is a driving movement secured when visibility is obscured?","An excavator has to maneuver behind an obstacle.","Drive without seeing the signaller’s signals.","If necessary, organize appropriate instruction with clear communication.","Only secure reversing by honking once.","Confusing routes require effective measures to prevent collisions and entrapment."],"b2-standplatz":["What applies to an excavator stand on a slope?","The floor is sloped and may be slippery.","The machine can extend as far as it likes at any inclination.","Always set up the excavator on a loose layer of earth.","Check the stability and operating limits of the machine before use.","Slope slope and subsoil have a significant influence on stability."],"b2-oberleitung":["Why does the distance of the boom from power lines need to be planned?","The boom can come close to the cable when swiveling.","Electrical flashover is also possible without direct contact.","Only the bucket can conduct electricity, not the boom.","With dry soil, every distance is automatically safe.","Limits of use and protective distances must be clarified before approaching electrical systems."],"b2-fremdperson":["A passer-by enters the construction site in the panning area. What is right?","The person suddenly stands near the excavator bucket.","Lift the shovel up and swing it over the person.","Stop movement immediately and have the area cleared.","Just continue to watch the person from the side window.","People in the danger area must not be endangered by work movements."],"b2-parkstellung":["How is an earthmoving machine secured after work is finished?","The excavator remains unattended on the construction site.","Leave the spoon at head height.","Let the engine run unattended.","Put down the work equipment, secure the machine and prevent unauthorized use.","Proper parking reduces accidental movement and unauthorized access."],"b2-eigenlast":["Why are equipment limits crucial when lifting with an excavator?","A heavy load is to be picked up on the boom.","Otherwise, stability and permissible load capacity may be exceeded.","Any machine can lift any load as long as the bucket fits.","Only the length of the sling rope determines the risk.","Lifting and load capacity information depends on the equipment and application situation."],"b2-untergrundhohlraum":["The floor above an old basement could be hollow. What are you doing?","You should drive the excavator into the area.","Cross the spot with maximum momentum.","Clarify load capacity and possible cavities before driving on.","Simply place a heavy load on the surface.","Cavities can collapse under the weight of the machine and cause the machine to crash."],"b2-feuchtigkeit":["After heavy rain the embankment becomes soft. What is right?","An excavator works near the edge of the embankment.","Move the machine closer to the edge to increase reach.","Ignore the changes until the end of the shift.","Reassess soil and stability conditions.","Moisture penetration can change the load-bearing capacity and stability of embankments."],"b2-bodenprobe":["Why do pipeline plans have to be checked before excavation?","Cables could run under the planned excavation.","So that lines can be identified and suitable security measures can be planned.","So that excavation can be carried out more quickly, independently of third-party systems.","Because machines must never be used near cables.","Underground supply lines require reliable location clarification before excavation work."],"b2-maschinenzugang":["What applies when getting in and out of the earthmoving machine?","The machine is on uneven terrain.","Slide down the hydraulic line out of the cab.","Use designated steps and ensure a secure footing.","Jump onto the swivel arm while the machine is running.","Safe climbs and suitable stopping points reduce the risk of falling and crushing."],"b2-kupplung":["How do you check a new backhoe after installation?","The bucket is connected via the quick coupler.","Only judge the spoon visually from a greater distance.","Step directly under the raised spoon.","Ensure correct locking and prescribed control steps.","Attachments that are incorrectly locked can come loose and endanger people."],"b2-hydraulikwartung":["Why are hydraulic lines not allowed to be opened under pressure?","A hose needs to be replaced.","Escaping fluid can cause serious injuries due to high pressure.","The pressure always prevents oil from escaping.","An open line can be safely checked with your hands.","High-pressure fluid can penetrate tissue and requires safe pressure relief."],"b2-fahrweg":["You have to drive over a temporary construction bridge. What are you checking?","The bridge is only designed for certain loads.","Whether the color of the bridge matches the machine.","Load capacity and suitability for the weight and dimensions of the machine.","Only whether a light car has already driven on the bridge.","Temporary structures may only be used within their proven load-bearing capacity."],"b2-baggertransport":["What is important when transporting an excavator on a low loader?","The machine is taken to the next construction site.","Allow the work equipment to protrude loosely over the edge.","Keep the cabin door open while driving.","Secure the machine according to transport specifications and check the loading equipment.","Transport locks and suitable loading facilities prevent slipping and falling."],"b2-schaufelfuellung":["Why is a wheel loader not allowed to drive fast with the bucket raised high?","The load is heavy and the ground is uneven.","A high center of gravity can increase the risk of tipping and visibility problems.","The bucket stabilizes automatically at high speeds.","The shovel height is irrelevant to stability.","A raised center of gravity typically worsens stability when driving and cornering."],"b2-fussgaenger":["How do you behave when maneuvering next to pedestrians?","The construction site access is also a footpath.","Use the shovel to direct pedestrians to the side.","Only carry out the driving movement when the area is safely clear and manageable.","Just honk once and drive on slowly without visibility.","Vehicle and passenger traffic must be effectively separated or safely coordinated."],"b2-ueberlastwarnung":["When lifting, the machine reports overload. What are you doing?","A lifted load reaches the permissible limits.","Switch off the warning and continue to raise it unchanged.","Tighten the load suddenly while the machine is running.","Stop dangerous movements and safely correct the load situation.","Overload warnings indicate possible limit violations and stability risks."],"b2-wasserleitung":["While digging, an unknown pipe is uncovered. What applies?","The line is not shown in the construction plans.","Stop work in the affected area and have the line identified professionally.","Try moving the line with the excavator shovel.","Continue digging directly under the line without checking.","Unknown lines can cause electrical, gas or water hazards."],"b2-hangefahrt":["How do you drive an excavator on a steep slope?","The planned route leads along a slope.","Drive across the slope regardless of the manufacturer's limits.","Observe the permissible inclination and prescribed driving style of the machine.","Swing the boom far out to balance the vehicle.","The permissible slope depends on the machine, the surface and the manufacturer's information."],"b2-schlechtebeleuchtung":["When working in a dark pit, visibility is inadequate. What is right?","You can hardly see people and obstacles.","Increase digging speed to complete the operation quickly.","Do not use the lights while the engine is running.","Stop work until the danger areas are sufficiently visible.","Safe visibility of driving and work areas is required for controlled machine movements."],"b2-kettenverschleiss":["During the daily check, a damaged caterpillar track is noticed. What are you doing?","A chain connection shows clear damage.","Do not continue to use the machine uncontrolled and report any damage.","Continue driving at high speed so that the chain straightens out.","Only continue working on soft ground without checking.","Damage to the drive can impair controllability and stability."],"b2-ladearbeiten":["You load a truck with the excavator. What is important?","The truck driver stays close to the loading area.","Swing the bucket over the unprotected driver's cab.","Prevent people from staying in the danger area and coordinate processes.","Begin loading without communicating with the driver.","When loading there is a risk of falling material and swinging movements."],"b2-arbeitsunterbrechung":["You interrupt excavation work for a meeting. What applies?","The machine should stand for several minutes without being operated.","Leave the lifted shovel as a marker.","Leave the machine unattended with the traction drive engaged.","Set down the implement safely and secure the machine against unintentional use.","Even short interruptions require a safe machine condition."],"b2-rollmaterial":["Loose material can fall when transported with the wheel loader. What is right?","The loader drives close to employees.","Pick up the load safely and choose a safe driving style with a suitable shovel position.","Raise the shovel as high as possible so that the surrounding area has a clear view.","Pick up the load without limiting the bucket filling.","Loose loads, high bucket positions and poor visibility can endanger people and traffic."]};
